# Platform support impersonation (P2-B)

Read-only operator session for platform ops (`owner` · `admin` · `support`) on **`{club}.admin.{PLATFORM_ROOT_DOMAIN}`** only. Denali workspace package is **not** modified — guards live in API middleware and web operator shell.

## Flow

```text
Super Admin (admin.{root})
  Owner tab → POST /platform/v1/tenants/:id/impersonate
  → audit IMPERSONATE_START
  → { sessionToken, exchangePath: "/auth/platform-impersonate", expiresAt }

Club admin host
  GET /auth/platform-impersonate#token=… (fragment removed from browser history before exchange)
  → POST /api/auth/platform-impersonate (web BFF)
  → POST /auth/accept-platform-impersonation (API verify JWT and atomically consume its jti)
  → Set-Cookie session (Max-Age=1800)
  → redirect /dashboard

Operator shell: data-operator-impersonation-banner; logout revokes the support session before
clearing the cookie. If the API is unavailable, the cookie is retained, the UI shows an error, and
the operator can retry. An API rejection means the token is already unusable and the cookie clears.
The session expires after 30 minutes. API ingress checks the session jti
against shared Redis and rejects revoked, missing, or unavailable support-session state; non-read
requests return 403 IMPERSONATION_READ_ONLY.
```

## API routes

| Method | Path                                              | Auth                        | Role                                                             |
| ------ | ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `POST` | `/platform/v1/tenants/{tenantId}/impersonate`     | platform ops Bearer + phone | `assertPlatformOpsImpersonateRole` (owner/admin/support)         |
| `POST` | `/platform/v1/tenants/{tenantId}/impersonate/end` | same                        | optional body `{ reason?: "manual" \| "timeout" \| "replaced" }` |
| `POST` | `/auth/accept-platform-impersonation`             | none (JWT in body)          | verifies impersonation JWT                                       |
| `POST` | `/auth/end-platform-impersonation`                | none (session JWT in body)  | revokes the verified session jti                                 |

### Start response (200)

```json
{
  "sessionToken": "<RS256 JWT>",
  "exchangePath": "/auth/platform-impersonate",
  "expiresAt": "<ISO-8601>"
}
```

JWT claims (30m expiry): `sub`, `tenant_id`, `role: "owner"`, `sess_ver`, `jti`, `platform_impersonation_readonly: true`, `platform_impersonator` (ops phone).

## Readonly guard

`assertOperatorImpersonationReadonly` runs at API ingress before route dispatch, independent of rate-limit configuration. Every request carrying a valid support JWT checks the jti against shared Redis; revoked or unavailable state fails closed. GET/HEAD pass after that check. Non-read requests with an active impersonation JWT → `ImpersonationReadOnlyError` → HTTP **403** `{ "error": "forbidden", "code": "IMPERSONATION_READ_ONLY" }`.

**Non-impersonation bearers:** when `AUTH_JWT_*` is configured, the guard must not `jwtVerify` unsigned
dev bearers (`dev.<base64url>`) or other non-RS256 tokens. Those are not platform impersonation
sessions — verify failure previously escaped as **500** `Invalid Compact JWS` on urban settings /
tour PATCH paths that already authenticated via `tryParseDevBearerToken`. Contract: skip
`DEV_BEARER_PREFIX` tokens; on any other verify failure, return (do not block the write). Only a
successfully verified JWT with `platform_impersonation_readonly: true` denies mutation.

## Audit

| Action              | When                                                               |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `IMPERSONATE_START` | successful start                                                   |
| `IMPERSONATE_END`   | `POST …/impersonate/end` (operator logout END audit deferred v1.1) |

The exchange token is passed in a URL fragment and removed before the request; Redis atomically
allows one exchange per jti. API ingress requires the exchange marker, so missing Redis state fails
closed. Operator logout revokes the session jti so copied tokens stop working. A failed request to
the API does not clear the session cookie or report success; the UI lets the operator retry. If
Redis is unavailable, support sessions fail closed.

## Platform billing vs Denali finance

Impersonation and platform billing (P2-C) do not touch `/finance/*` or `packages/workspaces/denali/**`.

